  "body": "Stacked on #4490 - do not merge before #4490.\n\n## What changed\n\nThis PR adds one Settings window for the per-user application settings (PR F1 of the UI plan #4245, design on #3025).\n\n- A new in-app window `settings_window.rs` with four sections:\n  - **Appearance:** theme and colour vision. A pick queues the same `SelectTheme` / `SelectColorVision` as the Theme door.\n  - **Graphics:** line width and anti-aliasing. They use the same `State` setters as before. An anti-aliasing count that the device does not offer stays disabled and says why.\n  - **Graphics device (read-only):** the adapter and the backend from the startup GPU line, and the sample counts that the device offers.\n  - **Updates:** \"Check for updates\".\n- Each choice applies at once and goes to `prefs.json` or `view.json`. Each section that holds a setting has \"Reset to defaults\". The file formats do not change.\n- The Settings button in the ribbon top band now opens and closes the window. The one-row Settings dropdown is removed.\n- The command table of #4490 gets one row: `file.settings`, \"Settings…\", in the File menu above Quit. It has no ribbon cell, because the top band button is the ribbon entry. `docs/decisions/4493-settings-window.md` gives the reasons.\n- The viewport Display menu loses the line width and the anti-aliasing. Its group \"Graphics\" is now \"View options\". The grid, the origin axes, the projection, the quality presets and the shading switches stay there as quick viewing toggles.\n- The window opening is view state (`State::settings_open`), as the ribbon doors are. No MCP tool and no CLI flag (answer 4 on #3025).\n\n## Screenshots (1366 x 768)\n\nBefore: the Settings dropdown.\n\n![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/refs/heads/pr-screenshots/4502/before-settings.png)\n\nAfter: the Settings window, Appearance and Graphics sections.\n\n![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/refs/heads/pr-screenshots/4502/after-settings.png)\n\n![after graphics](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/refs/heads/pr-screenshots/4502/after-graphics.png)\n\nBefore and after: the viewport Display menu.\n\n![before display](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/refs/heads/pr-screenshots/4502/before-display.png)\n\n![after display](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/refs/heads/pr-screenshots/4502/after-display.png)\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nNew, `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/settings_window.rs`:\n- `the_settings_button_opens_and_closes_the_window`\n- `the_menu_bar_settings_row_opens_the_window`\n- `appearance_picks_apply_at_once_are_kept_and_reset`\n- `graphics_reset_restores_the_line_width_and_the_antialiasing`\n- `the_graphics_device_section_is_read_only`\n- `updates_reset_turns_the_check_on_again`\n- `old_prefs_and_view_files_load_with_the_same_values`\n\nNew layout test: `layout_window_settings` (`tests/page_layout_windows.rs`).\n\nNew unit tests in `settings_window.rs`: `device_of_reads_the_adapter_and_the_backend`, `samples_line_joins_the_counts`.\n\nUpdated:\n- `layout_window_display_menu` (group \"View options\", no line width and anti-aliasing rows).\n- `the_display_button_opens_and_closes_the_menu_and_the_labels_exist` (the moved rows are not in the Display menu).\n- `display_quality.rs`: the line width and anti-aliasing tests now drive the Settings window; `the_graphics_group_offers_...` is renamed `the_settings_graphics_section_offers_the_line_widths_and_the_antialiasing`.\n- `update_check.rs`: `settings_toggle_persists_check_for_updates_and_hides_notice_without_dirtying_document` uses the window's Updates section.\n- The command table tests of #4490 read the new row from the table.\n\n`#[test]` count of `crates/ui`: 2027 before, 2037 after.\n\n## Gate\n\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base 3d75878691bd5617778c769d8c695791473a485a`, the head of #4490) and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`, on head `1ddcb82b10e75f0f8b0fad7d7818ffa21713a80e`: green (19 steps, 0 failed; the `ui suites: lib` step holds the new tests; the site tests step is SKIP on that lane because python, zola and node are missing, and this PR changes no site file); clippy clean. Log: `gate-4493-1ddcb82.log`.\n- No post, toolpath or project file change, so no example catalog suite applies. No light twin is touched.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The real GPU line on a native window: the tests set `gpu_line` by hand. The headless run has no GPU line, and the section then says \"Not known\".\n- The browser build: the Browse row of the theme list is disabled there by the same `browser_files::refusal` as in the Theme door; no test runs the wasm shell.\n\nChangelog: The Settings button and File > Settings… open one Settings window for theme, colour vision, line width, anti-aliasing, the graphics device and update checks. The line width and the anti-aliasing left the viewport Display menu.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #4493\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
